PegResponsiveIrm::setMarket(address)
├── given market is already set
│   ├── when the supplied market is zero, the existing market, or another non-zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with IrmMarketAlreadySet
│   ├── it should prioritize the already-set check over supplied-address validation
│   ├── it should leave market and the complete IRState unchanged
│   └── it should not emit events or make external calls
└── given market is not set
    ├── when the supplied market is the zero address
    │   ├── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── it should leave market and the complete IRState unchanged
    │   └── it should not emit events or make external calls
    └── when the supplied market is non-zero
        ├── when block.timestamp is greater than type(uint48).max
        │   ├── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast(48, block.timestamp)
        │   ├── it should roll back the market assignment and IRState changes
        │   └── it should not emit events
        └── when block.timestamp fits uint48
            ├── when block.timestamp is zero
            │   └── it should accept the minimum timestamp
            ├── when block.timestamp equals type(uint48).max
            │   └── it should accept the maximum uint48 timestamp
            ├── when caller is the owner, a non-owner, or differs from the supplied market
            │   └── it should allow the first caller because binding is permissionless
            ├── when the supplied market is an EOA or has no expected market interface
            │   └── it should accept the address without code or interface validation
            ├── it should set market to the supplied address exactly
            ├── it should set lastUpdate to block.timestamp
            ├── it should preserve borrowRate, recoveryStartedAt and stressMode
            ├── it should emit exactly IRStateUpdated with the complete resulting state
            ├── it should not read the oracle or call the supplied market
            └── it should make every later setMarket call revert with IrmMarketAlreadySet
